Description: watch a movie together from two homes, seeing and hearing each other
 Canape lets two people, each at home, watch a movie together while seeing
 and hearing each other. The movie stays on the server and each browser plays
 it by itself, straight from the server: there is no screen sharing, so the
 picture is as sharp at one end as at the other. Play, pause, seeking and the
 choice of the movie are shared and kept aligned. Cameras and microphones go
 through WebRTC, separately from the sound of the movie, so the film and the
 voices come out together.
 .
 It is a Node.js web server protected by one shared password, started as a
 system service ("canape.service") under its own "canape" user. The movies
 are read from /var/lib/canape/films, and the settings live in
 /etc/canape/canape.conf. A password and a secret for the session cookies are
 generated at the first installation, in /etc/canape/secrets.conf.
 .
 Camera and microphone need a secure page: HTTPS (reverse proxy such as
 Caddy or nginx) or localhost. Install ffmpeg to let the server check which
 movies every browser can play and to use "canape-convertir" on the others.
 .
 The package installs a signed APT repository entry, so "apt upgrade" keeps
 Canape up to date.
